KNOWNBUG
instance_array1.sv
--bound 1
^\[main\.s\[0\]\.p0\] always main\.s\[0\]\.bus\.v == 5: PROVED up to bound 1$
^\[main\.s\[1\]\.p0\] always main\.s\[1\]\.bus\.v == 5: PROVED up to bound 1$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Instance arrays of modules with interface ports are not supported.
expand_instance_array (src/verilog/verilog_elaborate_module_instances.cpp)
tries to split the port connection over the elements of the array, and
fails with "cannot split the connection over the 2 elements of the
instance array". Per 1800-2017 23.3.3, an interface instance that is
connected to an interface port of an instance array is connected to every
element of the array.
